
ValeVision3D - rotatable viewports

  The geometry (the real ViewportRotation leaf)
  PASS  an angle wraps into (-180, 180]
  PASS  Shift holds quarter turns counted from level
  PASS  free, it settles on a right angle within the detent and nowhere else
  PASS  the middle of the frame is what it turns about
  PASS  a quarter turn clockwise carries the level top-left corner to the top right of where it was (y runs down)
  PASS  ToFrame undoes ToPaper
  PASS  the turned corners, level top-left first
  PASS  the box round a quarter-turned frame is its height wide and its width tall
  PASS  a level frame's box is the frame itself
  PASS  a point inside the turned frame but outside the level one is inside
  PASS  and one inside the level frame but outside the turned one is not
  PASS  the distance to a turned frame is measured to its turned edge
  PASS  the CSS turn is nothing when level, and appended after the translate when turned
  PASS  a level viewport opens no graphics state
  PASS  a turned one opens one and writes one cm
  PASS  the matrix puts each level point where the turn puts it on the paper (to a hundredth of a point, 0.004 mm)

  The handles (the shipped ViewportHandles unit)
  PASS  the press remembers the turn, the middle and the angle it was grabbed at
  PASS  swung to due right: a quarter turn clockwise
  PASS  free, a hand a little past it stays where it is, to a tenth
  PASS  Shift holds it to the quarter turn
  PASS  Shift: swung round to straight down is a half turn (180, never -180), and round to the left a quarter turn back
  PASS  within the detent of a right angle it settles there without Shift
  PASS  too near the middle to read an angle, it holds still
  PASS  a turn is counted from where the viewport already stood
  PASS  the rotate grip stands straight out from the top edge, turned with the frame
  PASS  the grip is found at the handles' hit radius, and nowhere else
  PASS  dragging the turned right edge down the paper lengthens the frame along it
  PASS  and the edge opposite stays exactly where it was on the paper
  PASS  and the drawing stays put: the same drawing point is at the same paper point
  PASS  dragging it ACROSS the paper does nothing to that edge
  PASS  a level frame crops exactly as it always has
  PASS  a pan on a quarter-turned drawing slides it the way the hand went (down the paper is along its own x)
  PASS  a move is still a plain paper move, turned or not
  PASS  a 3D picture slides in the frame's own axes
  PASS  a handle's resize arrow turns with the frame
  PASS  and is the one it always was on a level frame
  PASS  the turned frame is hit where it is painted: a handle, the band, the inside

  The window and the snap index (the shipped units)
  PASS  a level window's ToPaper and ToFrame agree
  PASS  the drawing point at the window's middle is at the frame's middle, turned or not
  PASS  a turned window's ToPaper carries the turn, and FromPaper undoes it
  PASS  the window names its turn
  PASS  a turned drawing's line is filed where it is painted: 40 mm DOWN the paper from the middle, not across
  PASS  a line running off the level frame is clipped at the frame's own edge (and its half-millimetre pad), then turned

  The frame line and caption (the shipped SheetChrome unit, and jsPDF itself)
  PASS  a level viewport's frame line and caption are loose primitives, as they always were
  PASS  a turned one's are one group, turned about the middle of the frame
  PASS  built level inside it: the same primitives the level viewport gets
  PASS  on screen: one SVG rotate about the middle, round the lot
  PASS  a group with no turn is written exactly as before
  PASS  in the PDF: the graphics states balance
  PASS  and the turn is written as a cm of a 30 degree rotation
  PASS  before the frame's rectangle is drawn
  PASS  a level frame writes no cm at all

Every check passed.
